---
import DiagramFigure from './DiagramFigure.astro'

// The measured cost of a big auto-labeled set. Northcutt et al. (NeurIPS 2021)
// audited the test sets of ten of the most-cited ML benchmarks and found an
// average of at least 3.3% label errors, and once corrected, the rankings flip.
// One in thirty labels wrong, in the gold-standard sets, under years of scrutiny.
// The five hundred rows a model wrote you on Tuesday carry more.

const stats = [
  { value: '3.3%', label: 'avg label errors across 10 canonical benchmarks' },
  { value: '6%', label: 'of the ImageNet validation set' },
  { value: '1 in 30', label: 'gold-standard labels wrong' },
]
const pct = 3.3

const ariaLabel =
  'A measurement of label noise. Across the test sets of ten of the most-cited machine-learning benchmarks, an average of at least 3.3 percent of labels are wrong; ImageNet’s validation set is at least 6 percent wrong; roughly one in thirty gold-standard labels is incorrect. The bar shows 3.3 percent. The consequence: once enough mislabeled examples are corrected, model rankings flip, a model that looked better was only better at matching the errors.'
---

<DiagramFigure label="The cost of a big auto-labeled set" ariaLabel={ariaLabel} data-ln>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
    {
      stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="rounded border border-border-dark bg-surface-container-low px-4 py-4 text-center">
          <span class="block font-mono text-2xl text-error leading-none">{s.value}</span>
          <span class="block mt-2 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">{s.label}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <div class="mt-4">
    <div class="flex justify-between font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">
      <span>clean</span>
      <span>3.3% wrong, and it flips the rankings</span>
    </div>
    <div class="h-3 mt-1 rounded bg-surface-container-low overflow-hidden" role="presentation">
      <div class="ln-bar h-full" style={`width:${pct}%`}></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="note">
    These are the gold-standard sets the whole field ranks against, under years of
    scrutiny. The five hundred rows a model wrote for you on Tuesday carry more,
    and confident green over noisy labels is worse than honest red.
  </Fragment>
</DiagramFigure>

<style is:global>
  [data-ln] .ln-bar {
    min-width: 3px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-error) 70%, transparent);
    border-radius: 9999px;
  }
</style>
